(2907152, 403391, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by e301:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting; My first reaction is that the exposure lacks some control - has the impression of being brought back too far from over-exposed, or something, and I find the visibility of the cow''s shoulder unsettles the composition a bit - my eye can''t help but be pulled there - a slightly tighter crop might have made that balance more comfortable. background is something of a problem, not working with your subjects very happily; but the idea, overall, I like, and it''s been a lot more fun to look at than most. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>damn, that''s a good comment. wow, yes, I did bring it back from overexposed. you''ve done a great job of listing the problems of this shot. I just didn''t know how to overcome them.</td>', 'Originally posted by e301: Interesting; My first reaction is that the exposure lacks some control - has the impression of being brought back too far from over-exposed, or something, and I find the visibility of the cow''s shoulder unsettles the composition a bit - my eye can''t help but be pulled there - a slightly tighter crop might have made that balance more comfortable. background is something of a problem, not working with your subjects very happily; but the idea, overall, I like, and it''s been a lot more fun to look at than most.   damn, that''s a good comment. wow, yes, I did bring it back from overexposed. you''ve done a great job of listing the problems of this shot. I just didn''t know how to overcome them.', '2006-10-08 01:45:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2907166, 401238, 13077, '<td valign="top">Really good shot, nice job. Bear said it about the composition with the bike cropped off the bottom - the tight crop on the right is good, it creates visual tension that goes perfectly with the expression of the rider, and the overall shot. But, the bottom of tires and the ground they''re on are almost as important as the riders face in most MTB shots, IMO.</td>', 'Really good shot, nice job. Bear said it about the composition with the bike cropped off the bottom - the tight crop on the right is good, it creates visual tension that goes perfectly with the expression of the rider, and the overall shot. But, the bottom of tires and the ground they''re on are almost as important as the riders face in most MTB shots, IMO.', '2006-10-08 01:50:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2907167, 403796, 52336, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on top 50.. nice and peaceful image, with some lovely tack sharpness and interesting vignetting.  Colour choices are beautiful.  Nicely done.</td>', 'Congratulations on top 50.. nice and peaceful image, with some lovely tack sharpness and interesting vignetting.  Colour choices are beautiful.  Nicely done.', '2006-10-08 01:50:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(2907168, 403182, 50695, '<td valign="top">wow, I thought MY shot was underrated, but this takes the cake. <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=6999" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">e301</a> did an excellent job pointing out the technical problems with my picture, but I have no explanation for your score, except that people fear oblivion.</td>', 'wow, I thought MY shot was underrated, but this takes the cake.  e301 did an excellent job pointing out the technical problems with my picture, but I have no explanation for your score, except that people fear oblivion.', '2006-10-08 01:50:53.000000', NULL, 0),
