(2913669, 399950, 61679, '<td valign="top">Hello from the Critique Club,<br/> <br/>Wow, 22nd place out of 600+ entries and a 6.68 score.  Being just a registered member I couldn''t vote on this challenge but after reviewing the results, your image is a good as any of those in the top ten.  Looking at your profile, I expect to see a ribbon on your page in the very near future.<br/> <br/>This image suits my personal preference well, as I''m not a big fan of the hyper saturated look.  About the only suggestion I could make for improvement would be to clone out or burn the bright spot on the rock along the bottom edge.  My eyes were initially drawn there instead of to the wonderful birds sitting on the rocks.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique.<br/> <br/>Tim<br/></td>', 'Hello from the Critique Club, Wow, 22nd place out of 600+ entries and a 6.68 score.  Being just a registered member I couldn''t vote on this challenge but after reviewing the results, your image is a good as any of those in the top ten.  Looking at your profile, I expect to see a ribbon on your page in the very near future. This image suits my personal preference well, as I''m not a big fan of the hyper saturated look.  About the only suggestion I could make for improvement would be to clone out or burn the bright spot on the rock along the bottom edge.  My eyes were initially drawn there instead of to the wonderful birds sitting on the rocks. Feel free to PM me if you have any questions regarding this critique. Tim', '2006-10-10 08:51:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2913953, 404043, 32754, '<td valign="top">Remember, Shez, that this is photography and it is fun, creative and a learning experience: this is a very personal image, the kind that only you and those close to you can appreciate; it is intimate and touching...never let scores bother you; but sometimes it will hurt..just as some indiscreet comments can really hurt (I speak from experience). Always remember that it is an art form you seek and that you are an artist experimenting and perfecting your art...I''m glad you tried the sepia and b&amp;w...I would say that: the image appears over-saturated and a little over-processed...take more images of Peter and try different angles of light, see what happens...Marion</td>', 'Remember, Shez, that this is photography and it is fun, creative and a learning experience: this is a very personal image, the kind that only you and those close to you can appreciate; it is intimate and touching...never let scores bother you; but sometimes it will hurt..just as some indiscreet comments can really hurt (I speak from experience). Always remember that it is an art form you seek and that you are an artist experimenting and perfecting your art...I''m glad you tried the sepia and b&w...I would say that: the image appears over-saturated and a little over-processed...take more images of Peter and try different angles of light, see what happens...Marion', '2006-10-10 11:17:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914042, 399080, 66515, '<td valign="top">I see that many have sang your praise already and I''d like add my two bits to your already lengthy list of accolades. The surreal colors and the sharpness of this picture made it an immediate add to my favorite list. Thank you so much for this image.</td>', 'I see that many have sang your praise already and I''d like add my two bits to your already lengthy list of accolades. The surreal colors and the sharpness of this picture made it an immediate add to my favorite list. Thank you so much for this image.', '2006-10-10 11:46:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914099, 404080, 30508, '<td valign="top">Wow!  I guess I did miss the best falls.  I''m definitely going to have to go back there (but I guess I''ll need some L glass and a Canon to go with it!!!).</td>', 'Wow!  I guess I did miss the best falls.  I''m definitely going to have to go back there (but I guess I''ll need some L glass and a Canon to go with it!!!).', '2006-10-10 12:12:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914121, 402561, 64446, '<td valign="top">No doubt you''ve got the lights all right!<br/>I agree with hotpasta: one of the best portraits I''ve seen (on my favs too).<br/>Congratulations!</td>', 'No doubt you''ve got the lights all right!I agree with hotpasta: one of the best portraits I''ve seen (on my favs too).Congratulations!', '2006-10-10 12:26:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914125, 403981, 40718, '<td valign="top">The technicals: You did well not to oversaturate the sky and get pixelation.  The rays from the sun was a good idea.  Having a foreground subject is good in landscape, but I''m not sure I would have chosen this one.  Pines just are hard to photograph, period.  The biggest downside, and one which immediately caught my eye, is the texture of the water.  I don''t think it''s good.  It''s probably a product of being in no-man''s land as far as shutter speed.  Not fast enough to freeze the water, not slow enough to blur it.  There are halos from PP which some people may have caught. (see the back trees<br/> <br/>The feel: has a nice sunset feel.  Things that would boost the score (but you have no control over) would be clouds in the sky to add interest and a more interesting foreground subject.</td>', 'The technicals: You did well not to oversaturate the sky and get pixelation.  The rays from the sun was a good idea.  Having a foreground subject is good in landscape, but I''m not sure I would have chosen this one.  Pines just are hard to photograph, period.  The biggest downside, and one which immediately caught my eye, is the texture of the water.  I don''t think it''s good.  It''s probably a product of being in no-man''s land as far as shutter speed.  Not fast enough to freeze the water, not slow enough to blur it.  There are halos from PP which some people may have caught. (see the back trees The feel: has a nice sunset feel.  Things that would boost the score (but you have no control over) would be clouds in the sky to add interest and a more interesting foreground subject.', '2006-10-10 12:27:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914134, 403827, 40718, '<td valign="top">Technicals: good focus and composition.  The shot is, in general, overexposed.  You may have been able to rescue it with a lowering of midtones in PS.<br/> <br/>The feel:  I like the square crop and the closed in composition.  The primarily diagonal lines also add to a feel of dynamics.  This is the strength of the shot.  The selective desat isn''t bad and I tend to like the technique, but you always need to ask what the purpose is.  I think the blue of your eyes works to draw us to them, but the green of the hat? I''m neutral about it.<br/> <br/>The game: I think you got a bit hosed on votes.  This is a better shot than the score.  The overexposure, to me, is the most obvious weakness.</td>', 'Technicals: good focus and composition.  The shot is, in general, overexposed.  You may have been able to rescue it with a lowering of midtones in PS. The feel:  I like the square crop and the closed in composition.  The primarily diagonal lines also add to a feel of dynamics.  This is the strength of the shot.  The selective desat isn''t bad and I tend to like the technique, but you always need to ask what the purpose is.  I think the blue of your eyes works to draw us to them, but the green of the hat? I''m neutral about it. The game: I think you got a bit hosed on votes.  This is a better shot than the score.  The overexposure, to me, is the most obvious weakness.', '2006-10-10 12:32:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914203, 402572, 40718, '<td valign="top">4.9? Wow.  A bit hammered on that.<br/> <br/>Technicals:  Focus is good.  Lighting is good.  Composition is good.  Screw anybody who knicked you for cutting off the wing.  It can be just as easily said that it provides the impression of the butterfly not being contained by frame and is ready to spring off the screen.<br/> <br/>The feel/the game: I think the shot probably just didn''t "wow" people in a 600 entry challenge.  Note the 88 5s you got.  That, to me, signifies people looking for literally 2-3 seconds and saying, "this picture isn''t bad (so I can''t give 4 or less), but it doesn''t do too much for me (so I can''t give 6 or more). 5".  I sorta agree.  The canvas is a bit stark, which isn''t bad, but also doesn''t hold our attention too long.</td>', '4.9? Wow.  A bit hammered on that. Technicals:  Focus is good.  Lighting is good.  Composition is good.  Screw anybody who knicked you for cutting off the wing.  It can be just as easily said that it provides the impression of the butterfly not being contained by frame and is ready to spring off the screen. The feel/the game: I think the shot probably just didn''t "wow" people in a 600 entry challenge.  Note the 88 5s you got.  That, to me, signifies people looking for literally 2-3 seconds and saying, "this picture isn''t bad (so I can''t give 4 or less), but it doesn''t do too much for me (so I can''t give 6 or more). 5".  I sorta agree.  The canvas is a bit stark, which isn''t bad, but also doesn''t hold our attention too long.', '2006-10-10 13:00:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(2914309, 398283, 16241, '<td valign="top">did i forget to congratulate you???  i still wanna go there, so purdy.</td>', 'did i forget to congratulate you???  i still wanna go there, so purdy.', '2006-10-10 14:06:28.000000', NULL, 0),
