(2944323, 399278, 20530, '<td valign="top"><img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_N.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=39850" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">macrothing</a>already nailed everything I was going to say. I also wonder if it would benefit to straighten out the lines of the wall with the transform tool? They are off just enough to be a slight distraction, but not enough to appear intentional.<br/> <br/>I really like this. You have a great eye for color and grungy processing. The image is interesting, balanced and has a lot of depth. Great work.<br/> <br/>It''s also thrilling to see that you got many referrals from this shot! Congrats! I think you''ll do very well as a band photographer.</td>', ' macrothingalready nailed everything I was going to say. I also wonder if it would benefit to straighten out the lines of the wall with the transform tool? They are off just enough to be a slight distraction, but not enough to appear intentional. I really like this. You have a great eye for color and grungy processing. The image is interesting, balanced and has a lot of depth. Great work. It''s also thrilling to see that you got many referrals from this shot! Congrats! I think you''ll do very well as a band photographer.', '2006-10-19 15:19:10.000000', NULL, 0),
